(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// The module array (PY6d, the data family; Modules/arraymodule.c of CPython 3.14.10, ported method by"] [11 1 "// method with its messages): array.array over the machine values of its type code (b B u w h H i I l L q Q"] [12 1 "// f d, 64-bit Linux's sizes, wchar_t 4 bytes, little-endian on both targets) held as bytes, a bytes-like"] [13 1 "// object (its buffer is the array's bytes); its sequence, comparison, concatenation and repetition"] [14 1 "// protocols, slices with steps (get, set, delete), every method of arraymodule.c (append, buffer_info,"] [15 1 "// byteswap, clear, count, extend, frombytes, fromfile, fromlist, fromunicode, index, insert, pop, remove,"] [16 1 "// reverse, tobytes, tofile, tolist, tounicode, __copy__, __deepcopy__, __reduce_ex__, __sizeof__,"] [17 1 "// __class_getitem__), its iterator (array.arrayiterator: __reduce__, __setstate__) and"] [18 1 "// _array_reconstructor (pickling by machine format code). Registered with collections.abc.MutableSequence."] [19 1 "// The buffer's export count (queue 249, buffer_export.go): a resize while a memoryview holds the array raises"] [20 1 "// BufferError, as array_resize and the slice assignments' early checks (issue #4509) do."] [29 12 "// the item size"] [31 14 "// the type made (a subclass's), for repr"] [32 14 "// the items allocated (array_resize's growth), for __sizeof__"] [33 2 "// exports is ob_exports (queue 249): the memoryviews holding the buffer"] [37 1 "// Exports makes an array a counting exporter (buffer_export.go)."] [42 1 "// refuseResize is the early check of issue #4509: a size change refused before anything moves."] [47 1 "// BufferFormat is array_buffer_getbuf's format (queue 304): the typecode, 'w' for 'u' (Py_UNICODE_WIDE); 'u' and 'w'"] [48 1 "// stay byte views here (memoryview has no unpacking of them: CPython's tolist raises NotImplementedError), and 3.15's"] [49 1 "// complex codes their \"Zf\" and \"Zd\"."] [52 17 "// queue 473: Py_UCS4's \"w\", its itemsize the array's (BufferItemsize); memoryview has no unpacking of it"] [60 1 "// BufferItemsize is the itemsize of the array's Py_buffer (queue 473: a format memoryview does not know, \"w\")."] [63 1 "// BytesLike makes an array a bytes-like object: its buffer, not copied."] [67 17 "// nil once exhausted"] [78 1 "// arrayTypecodes315 are 3.15.2's typecodes (arraymodule.c's descriptors, queue 263): its 'e' (half float), 'Zf' and 'Zd'"] [79 1 "// (complex), held as the codes e, F and D; the module's typecodes a tuple of them."] [82 1 "// arrayCodeOf is a 3.15.2 typecode's code, 0 when it names none."] [96 1 "// arrayTypecodeName is a code's typecode: \"Zf\" and \"Zd\" for the complex codes (queue 263)."] [107 1 "// arrayComplexArg is cf_setitem's and cd_setitem's PyArg_Parse \"D;array item must be complex\" (PyComplex_AsCComplex:"] [108 1 "// a value that is no number fails in PyFloat_AsDouble, \"must be real number, not T\", as 3.15.2's oracle shows)."] [133 1 "// resize is array_resize: n items; the allocation follows arraymodule.c's growth pattern (for __sizeof__),"] [134 1 "// the bytes past the old length are the caller's to fill; refused (BufferError) while the buffer is exported and the"] [135 1 "// size changes."] [169 1 "// get is the descriptor's getitem."] [197 12 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's e_getitem, cf_getitem, cd_getitem"] [204 2 "// u, w: a code point (any 32-bit value, as PyUnicode_FromOrdinal: out of range a ValueError's"] [205 2 "// territory, never reached from Python)"] [236 1 "// encode is the descriptor's setitem without the store: v's machine value, or CPython's error."] [346 12 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's e_setitem: the float as a C float, then PyFloat_Pack2"] [393 1 "// ins is ins1: v checked, then inserted before where."] [491 1 "// dataEq is PyObject_RichCompareBool(a, b, Py_EQ): identity first."] [503 1 "// dataWarn is PyErr_WarnEx: warnings.warn(msg, category, stacklevel)."] [506 52 "// _warnings' own path at shutdown (queue 253)"] [626 1 "// mformat codes (arraymodule.c's enum machine_format_code)"] [646 2 "// 3.15.2's (queue 263)"] [697 1 "// arrayNew is array_new: array(typecode[, initializer]) of type t."] [712 15 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's array_new parses \"s|O:array\": a typecode of any length"] [804 28 "// newarrayobject's exact size"] [903 2 "// issue #4509: a size change refused before the array is touched"] [923 3 "// delete the extended slice"] [1091 2 "// the number protocol's special methods as attributes (CPython's slot wrappers of sq_concat, sq_repeat,"] [1092 2 "// sq_inplace_concat, sq_inplace_repeat)"] [1107 78 "// sq_repeat's wrapper"] [1148 3 "// the address: a stable number of the buffer (pyi has no pointers); 0 for an empty array, as CPython's"] [1159 40 "// 3.15.2: a complex's two halves swapped each"] [1212 3 "// the argument's buffer held over the call (Py_buffer): a.frombytes(a) is refused as a resize while exported"] [1265 32 "// the old size: never refused"] [1348 19 "// the subclass's instance: its __dict__ is the state"] [1425 3 "// _PyObject_SIZE(array) on 64-bit CPython 3.14: 64 bytes, then the allocated items"] [1484 16 "// 3.15.2: a tuple of the typecodes"] [1509 1 "// sliceIndexArg is clinic's slice_index(accept={int}): an int clipped to the index range."] [1527 1 "// arrayReconstructor is array__array_reconstructor_impl."] [1545 15 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's typecode: str, and the machine codes 22-27"] [1590 107 "// 3.15.2's"] [1688 1 "// callBytesDecode is bytes.decode(enc) through the bytes type's method."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[110 26] [119 28] [139 29] [409 27] [430 29] [455 42] [482 35] [505 25] [526 12] [526 19] [607 12] [607 38] [738 118] [744 29] [747 32] [761 33] [779 29] [785 29] [790 29] [794 29] [808 29] [816 12] [816 24] [826 25] [837 23] [837 30] [861 25] [905 29] [913 47] [925 23] [925 40] [929 13] [929 24] [940 22] [940 39] [960 13] [960 24] [978 14] [978 25] [979 49] [1036 13] [1036 20] [1055 44] [1081 33