;; The module array (PY6d, the data family; Modules/arraymodule.c of CPython 3.14.10, ported method by
;; method with its messages): array.array over the machine values of its type code (b B u w h H i I l L q Q
;; f d, 64-bit Linux's sizes, wchar_t 4 bytes, little-endian on both targets) held as bytes, a bytes-like
;; object (its buffer is the array's bytes); its sequence, comparison, concatenation and repetition
;; protocols, slices with steps (get, set, delete), every method of arraymodule.c (append, buffer_info,
;; byteswap, clear, count, extend, frombytes, fromfile, fromlist, fromunicode, index, insert, pop, remove,
;; reverse, tobytes, tofile, tolist, tounicode, __copy__, __deepcopy__, __reduce_ex__, __sizeof__,
;; __class_getitem__), its iterator (array.arrayiterator: __reduce__, __setstate__) and
;; _array_reconstructor (pickling by machine format code). Registered with collections.abc.MutableSequence.
;; The buffer's export count (queue 249, buffer_export.go): a resize while a memoryview holds the array raises
;; BufferError, as array_resize and the slice assignments' early checks (issue #4509) do.

